    "created_at": "2026-07-13T23:02:03Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-07-13T23:02:03Z",
    "body": "> I think this is overly complex and we can instead say that `document.open` always supports DSD, which makes it so that we don't need to keep a flag on the document.\n\nIt seems ok to me, except that part of the point was to disallow *any* legacy methods from using DSD, for security. That included `document.open/write`. Perhaps it's fine though?",
